\section{Introduction}
Feroge (also Ferroge, Feroghe, Kaligi; ISO 639-3 fer) is spoken in Western Bahr el Ghazal state, South Sudan. Sources found describe it as unwritten and shifting, with Arabic widely used alongside it. Little exists beyond encyclopedic and classification pages; no teaching materials were found.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
None found.

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Kaligi language (Wikipedia): \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kaligi_language}
\item Glottolog entry for Feroge: \url{https://glottolog.org/resource/languoid/id/fero1244.bigmap.html}
\item Feroge numerals page, Max Planck Institute for Evolutionary Anthropology: \url{https://lingweb.eva.mpg.de/channumerals/Feroge.htm}
\end{itemize}

\section{Religious and Community Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Joshua Project language page for Feroge (demographic information only): \url{https://joshuaproject.net/languages/fer}
\end{itemize}

\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
None found.

\section{Curriculum Development Context}
The language is reported as unwritten, so any curriculum would first require an orthography and basic documentation. No schooling in Feroge was found.

\end{document}
